<SiteLayout page="home">
<section class="hero section-wrap"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> PERSONAL · PROFESSIONAL · CREATIVE</p><h1>Technology with a <em>human</em> perspective.</h1><p class="hero-intro">I'm Kastine Augak — a Ugandan technology builder interested in useful software, accessible innovation, local languages, music and the communities around them.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="mailto:kastineaugak@gmail.com">Start a conversation <span>↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="biography.html">A little more about me <span>→</span></a></div><div class="hero-meta"><span class="status-dot"></span><span>Based in Fort Portal, Uganda</span><span class="meta-divider">/</span><span>Technology &amp; media</span></div></div>
<div class="hero-visual"><div class="portrait-frame"><img src={portrait} alt="Portrait of Kastine Augak" width="560" height="560" fetchpriority="high"><div class="portrait-caption"><span>01 / THE PERSON</span><span>Curious by nature.</span></div></div><div class="visual-note"><span class="note-mark">✳</span><span>Ideas become<br>useful things.</span></div></div><div class="hero-index">KA — 001</div></section>
<section class="intro-band section-wrap" id="about"><div class="section-kicker">01 / A SHORT INTRODUCTION</div><div class="intro-content"><h2>One person, <span>many interests.</span></h2><div><p>My work sits where software, learning and everyday life meet. I enjoy exploring how technology can solve practical problems — especially when the solution respects local context, limited connectivity and the people who use it.</p><a class="text-link" href="biography.html">Read my biography <span>→</span></a></div></div></section>
<section class="focus-section section-wrap"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / WHAT I CARE ABOUT</p><h2>Areas of focus</h2></div><p class="section-aside">A broad practice shaped by curiosity, experimentation and real-world needs.</p></div><div class="focus-grid">
<article class="focus-item"><span class="item-number">01</span><div><h3>Software &amp; systems</h3><p>Designing and building digital products, web experiences and practical tools with an eye on reliability and usability.</p></div><span class="item-arrow">↗</span></article>
<article class="focus-item"><span class="item-number">02</span><div><h3>AI &amp; local learning</h3><p>Exploring useful applications of AI, educational technology and language-aware experiences for East African communities.</p></div><span class="item-arrow">↗</span></article>
<article class="focus-item"><span class="item-number">03</span><div><h3>Research &amp; ideas</h3><p>Learning in public, investigating emerging technology and turning questions into clear, useful explanations.</p></div><span class="item-arrow">↗</span></article>
<article class="focus-item"><span class="item-number">04</span><div><h3>Music &amp; community</h3><p>Making room for creative practice, collaboration, music and the communities that make it meaningful.</p></div><span class="item-arrow">↗</span></article></div></section>
<section class="ventures-section section-wrap" id="ventures"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">03 / SELECTED WORK</p><h2>Projects &amp; ventures</h2></div><p class="section-aside">A selection of initiatives connected to my work and interests.</p></div><div class="venture-grid">
<article class="venture-card venture-feature"><div class="venture-top"><span>01 — EDUCATION &amp; AI</span><span class="venture-symbol">↗</span></div><h3>SomaGPT</h3><p>An education-focused AI initiative exploring how digital learning support can better serve students and local language contexts.</p><a href="https://somagtp.netlify.app/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Visit SomaGPT <span>↗</span></a></article>
<article class="venture-card"><div class="venture-top"><span>02 — DIGITAL SERVICES</span><span class="venture-symbol">↗</span></div><h3>Apex Web Services</h3><p>A web and digital services venture focused on helping people and organizations establish a useful online presence.</p><span class="quiet-note">Project information available on request</span></article>
<article class="venture-card venture-muted"><div class="venture-top"><span>03 — PERSONAL RESEARCH</span><span class="venture-symbol">↗</span></div><h3>Language &amp; access</h3><p>Ongoing interest in language technology, digital inclusion and software that works in low-bandwidth environments.</p><a href="blog.html">Explore journal notes <span>→</span></a></article></div></section>
<section class="personal-section section-wrap" id="interests"><div class="personal-copy"><p class="eyebrow">04 / BEYOND THE SCREEN</p><h2>Technology is part of life. <em>Not all of it.</em></h2><p>Music, collaboration and community are important parts of how I learn and see the world. I play instruments including tenor trombone and saxophone, and value the discipline and teamwork that creative practice teaches.</p><a class="text-link" href="biography.html#interests">More about my interests <span>→</span></a></div><div class="personal-note"><span class="quote-mark">“</span><p>Stay curious. Make things that matter. Keep learning.</p><span class="note-credit">A WORKING PRINCIPLE</span></div></section>
